},{"label":"Not diluting shareholders","ok":true,"evidence":"Diluted share count -2.1% YoY"},{"label":"Analyst estimates moving higher","ok":null,"evidence":"Estimate-revision feed not connected (Phase 2)"},{"label":"Management guidance increasing","ok":null,"evidence":"Earnings Intelligence Engine not built (Phase 2)"}],"thesis":"Apple (AAPL) screens at opportunity 65.0 with an expectations gap of 7.0. Reality 67.0 reflects +14.2% TTM revenue growth, +33.2% operating margin and +111.5% ROIC; pricing 60.0 reflects a fair multiple and strong price momentum. Primary theme exposure: Edge AI (trend 60.0). Macro fit for Technology in a Goldilocks regime is 53.0/100.","market_expectation":{"summary":"Priced roughly in line with its own history and peers; the market expects the current trajectory to continue.","evidence":["EV/Sales 10.5x (86.0th pct of own 5y range)","P/E 38x (43.0th pct of own history)","FCF yield 2.8%","PEG 1.2","12m return +32%, -1% from 52w high"]},"what_market_misses":["Operating leverage is showing up in margins faster than in the valuation."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (roughly 90 days after the last filing on 2026-07-31)","Edge AI: evidence that 'Power-efficient silicon, on-device memory' is easing via NPUs in phones/PCs/cars, low-power memory","Continued rotation into Technology"],"risks":["No engine-flagged risks; standard execution and macro risk apply."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 9% (currently 14.2%)","ROIC falls below 84% (currently 111.5%)","Operating margin compresses more than 200 bps YoY (currently 33.2%)","Technology rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs (currently +66)","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55%","Price closes >10% below its 200-day average with negative relative strength","Edge AI theme trend drops below 45"],"break_rules":[{"id":"revenue_growth","label":"TTM revenue growth","metric":"revenue_growth","op":"<","threshold":0.0924,"current":0.1424},{"id":"roic","label":"ROIC","metric":"roic","op":"<","threshold":0.8363,"current":1.1151},{"id":"margin","label":"Operating margin change YoY","metric":"operating_margin_change","op":"<","threshold":-0.02,"current":0.013065773311612072},{"id":"rotation","label":"Technology rotation score","metric":"sector_rotation","op":"<","threshold":-20,"consecutive":2,"current":66.0},{"id":"regime","label":"P(Stagflation)+P(Contraction)","metric":"adverse_regime_prob","op":">","threshold":55,"current":48.9},{"id":"trend","label":"Distance from 200dma","metric":"dist_200dma","op":"<","threshold":-10,"and_negative_rs":true,"current":16.9},{"id":"theme","label":"Edge AI theme trend","metric":"theme_trend","theme_id":"edge-ai","op":"<","threshold":45,"current":60.0}],"narrative_note":"Narrative from the last 7 morning briefs' theme signals (exposure-weighted).","llm_enriched":true,"theme_exposures":[{"theme_id":"edge-ai","theme":"Edge AI","weight":0.3,"order":1,"effective":0.3}],"llm":{"thesis":"Apple is compounding at a rate that is atypical for its size: TTM revenue of $466.8B growing +14.2% and accelerating from +12.8%, operating margin up 131bps to 33.2%, and FCF up +42.1% to $136.7B on a 29.3% FCF margin. The important dislocation is inside the multiple itself \u2014 EV/Sales sits at the 86th percentile of its own 5-year range while P/E sits at only the 43rd percentile, which means the market is paying a record price per dollar of revenue but a merely average price per dollar of earnings. That gap is the arithmetic signature of margin expansion and a -2.1% diluted share count doing the work that multiple expansion used to do, and it is the cleanest expression of the engine's +7.0 expectations gap. The setup is not 'cheap' \u2014 it is 'earnings are catching up to a price that already moved +32% in twelve months.' The trade is owning operating leverage that is showing up in the income statement faster than in the earnings multiple, with the caveat that the sales multiple offers essentially no valuation cushion if growth decelerates.","fundamental_read":"Growth is accelerating (+14.2% vs +12.8% prior) at a $467B revenue base, which is the single most unusual datapoint here and implies a genuine hardware refresh cycle rather than pricing alone. Profitability is exceptional and improving: 48.7% gross margin, 33.2% operating margin (+131bps YoY), 27.6% net margin, 106% FCF conversion, and ROIC of 111.5% \u2014 though incremental ROIC of 80.8% is below the trailing level, meaning new capital is earning less than the installed base, which is the first quiet crack in the quality story. The balance sheet is effectively unlevered at 0.12x net debt/EBITDA with $62.4B cash, and capital return is heavy ($82.2B buybacks, $15.6B dividends, 2.0% shareholder yield). Capex of $10.0B on $146.7B operating cash flow is strikingly asset-light for a company positioning into on-device AI \u2014 Apple is renting the AI capital intensity from its supply chain rather than owning it.","technical_read":"Trend is intact and orderly rather than parabolic: price 335.92 above SMA20 (328), SMA50 (322) and SMA200 (287), with a 50>200 uptrend and MACD histogram positive at +0.81. RSI 61.3 is constructive and not overbought despite sitting -1.2% from the 52-week high, which suggests the +8.4% one-month move was absorbed without exhaustion. The vulnerability is extension: 16.9% above the 200-day is a wide gap, so a growth or margin disappointment has roughly 15% of air beneath it before trend support engages.","market_expectation":"At 38x earnings, 29.3x EV/EBITDA, 10.5x EV/Sales and a 2.8% FCF yield with PEG of 1.2, the market expects mid-teens revenue growth and 33%+ operating margins to persist \u2014 it is extrapolating the current trajectory, not underwriting a step-change. The 86th percentile EV/Sales says investors have already accepted that Apple deserves a higher price per revenue dollar because that revenue is now more profitable; the 43rd percentile P/E says they have not yet paid a premium for the possibility that margins keep expanding. In short: the market has priced the margin level, not the margin slope.","what_market_misses":["The EV/Sales vs P/E percentile spread (86th vs 43rd) is the whole thesis in one number \u2014 the market is valuing Apple as a richer revenue stream but an average earnings stream, so continued operating leverage accrues to the P/E rather than requiring new multiple expansion.","Revenue acceleration at a $467B base is mathematically rare and is not typically what a 43rd-percentile earnings multiple prices; the market appears to be treating +14.2% as a cyclical spike rather than a cycle.","Apple's asset-light path into Edge AI ($10B capex on $147B operating cash flow) means it captures AI monetization without the depreciation drag weighing on hyperscaler free cash flow \u2014 a relative FCF advantage that screens poorly on 'AI capex commitment' narratives.","Buybacks of $82.2B against a $4.9T cap are retiring 2.1% of shares annually, converting ~30% net income growth into ~32% EPS growth; this is a durable, non-narrative source of per-share compounding.","Incremental ROIC (80.8%) running below trailing ROIC (111.5%) is the one deteriorating internal metric and is not visible in headline quality screens \u2014 it hints the marginal dollar of investment is less productive than the legacy base."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (~90 days after the 2026-07-31 filing) \u2014 the key line is whether operating margin holds above 33% while revenue growth stays double-digit; a third consecutive acceleration would force the earnings multiple higher.","Evidence that the Edge AI constraint \u2014 power-efficient silicon and on-device memory \u2014 is easing via next-gen NPUs and low-power memory, which would extend the device refresh cycle Apple is currently monetizing.","Continued capital rotation into Technology (+66 score vs every other sector negative except Energy at +27) supplying passive and momentum flows.","Continued buyback execution at current scale, which compounds EPS roughly 2%/year independent of operating results."],"risks":["EV/Sales at the 86th percentile of its 5-year range leaves no valuation cushion \u2014 a revenue deceleration back toward high single digits would compress both the sales and earnings multiples simultaneously.","Technology rotation at +66 while nine of eleven sectors are deeply negative is a crowded, one-sided positioning regime; crowding unwinds hit the largest index weight hardest.","The regime read is effectively uninformative (Goldilocks 26.6%, Reflation 24.6%, Contraction 25.4%, Stagflation 23.5% \u2014 near-uniform), and macro fit is only 53/100, so the macro overlay provides no support to the thesis.","Price is 16.9% above the 200-day; mean reversion alone could produce a double-digit drawdown without any change in fundamentals.","Evidence coverage is 0.75 \u2014 estimate revisions and management guidance feeds are not connected, so the thesis rests on reported financials and price behavior without a forward-expectations check.","Incremental ROIC below trailing ROIC suggests the marginal return on invested capital is fading even as headline quality looks pristine."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 9% (currently 14.2%), removing the acceleration premise.","Operating margin compresses more than 200bps YoY from 33.2%, breaking the operating-leverage mechanism.","EV/Sales percentile exceeds ~95th while P/E percentile converges above the 70th \u2014 at that point the margin re-rating is fully priced and the asymmetry is gone.","ROIC falls below 84%, or incremental ROIC falls below ~50%, signalling capital productivity decay.","Buyback pace slows materially such that diluted share count stops shrinking ~2%/year.","Price closes >10% below the 200-day average with negative relative strength.","Technology rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs (currently +66), or Edge AI theme trend drops below 45."],"second_order_beneficiaries":["Low-power memory suppliers (LPDDR/on-device DRAM and NAND): the engine explicitly names 'on-device memory' as the binding Edge AI constraint, and Apple's device volumes at 14%+ revenue growth pull content per unit higher.","Leading-edge foundry and advanced packaging: Apple's $10B capex vs $147B operating cash flow means the silicon capital intensity is borne by its manufacturing partners, who capture the fab utilization and pricing power.","NPU/IP licensing and EDA vendors supplying the power-efficient inference blocks that make on-device AI feasible \u2014 they monetize the constraint regardless of which handset OEM wins.","Thermal management, power delivery and advanced substrate suppliers: pushing inference onto battery-powered devices is fundamentally a joules-per-token problem, and the physical components that solve it see content gains.","Index and passive complex plus options market-makers: at a $4.9T cap with sector rotation at +66, Apple flow mechanically drives Technology-weighted vehicles."],"epistemic_labels":[{"statement":"TTM revenue of $466.8B grew +14.2%, accelerating from +12.8% in the prior quarter.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Operating margin is 33.2%, up 131bps YoY; FCF is $136.7B, up +42.1%, at a 29.3% FCF margin.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"ROIC is 111.5% while incremental ROIC is 80.8%; net debt/EBITDA is 0.12x; diluted shares fell 2.1% YoY on $82.2B of buybacks.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"EV/Sales is at the 86th percentile of its 5-year range while P/E (38x) is at the 43rd percentile; FCF yield 2.8%, PEG 1.2.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Price is 335.92, above the 20/50/200-day averages, 16.9% above the 200-day, RSI 61.3, MACD positive, -1.2% from the 52-week high, +32% over 12 months.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"The market expects the current growth and margin trajectory to continue and is priced roughly in line with its own history and peers.","kind":"consensus_expectation"},{"statement":"The gap between an 86th-percentile EV/Sales and a 43rd-percentile P/E is the arithmetic signature of margin expansion, meaning further operating leverage accrues to the earnings multiple without requiring new multiple expansion.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Revenue acceleration at a $467B base implies a genuine hardware refresh cycle rather than price/mix alone.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Capex of $10B against $147B operating cash flow means Apple is capturing on-device AI monetization while outsourcing the capital intensity to its supply chain, yielding a relative FCF advantage versus capex-heavy AI peers.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Technology rotation at +66 against nine negative sectors represents crowded positioning that would hit the largest index weight hardest in an unwind.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"An easing of the power-efficient-silicon and on-device-memory constraint would extend the current device refresh cycle and sustain double-digit revenue growth into subsequent quarters.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"Incremental ROIC falling below trailing ROIC is an early signal of capital productivity decay that will eventually pressure the quality premium.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"The near-uniform regime probability distribution (26.6/24.6/25.4/23.5) means the macro overlay carries no usable information for this thesis.","kind":"ai_inference"}],"confidence":0.56}},"technical":{"score":100,"passes":8,"criteria":{"above_150_200":true,"150_above_200":true,"200_rising_1m":true,"50_above_150_200":true,"above_50":true,"25pct_above_52w_low":true,"within_25pct_of_52w_high":true,"rs_positive_6m":true},"ready":true,"stage":"stage2_uptrend","close":335.92,"sma50":321.68,"sma150":294.47,"sma200":287.45,"sma150_prev4w":285.96,"sma150_declining":false,"pct_above_52w_low":37.0,"pct_from_52w_high":-1.2,"rs_6m":13.9,"rsi14":61.3,"atr20":7.2